{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1089162-developing-a-bloodline-delilah","id":1089162,"title":"Developing a Bloodline: Delilah","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T08:17:21-07:00","id":1089162,"title":"Developing a Bloodline: Delilah","content":"Developing a new bloodline for an Elder and her progeny in my chronicle. Looking for opinions particularly on the balance of the devotions<br /> <br /> Delilah<br /> The Delilah bloodline is a young bloodline made by an elder in New York. The Delilah draws on their beast, allowing it to inspire their creativity and art. From this they know how to make paints infused with vitae allowing them to work unique devotions through their artwork. However the beast's whispers into their artisic mindset unhinges their mind causing them to become quite mad.<br /> Clan: Daeva<br /> Nickname: the Painters<br /> Bloodline Bane: The painters suffer from an inherant madness welling up from allowing the beast to influence their creativity. They have the persistant Madness condition and it cannot be resolved.<br /> Bloodline Disciplines: Auspex, Celerity, Majesty, Vigor<br /> <br /> Devotions<br /> <br /> Truth in Art<br /> Roll: Intelligence+Crafts+Blood Potency taking 1 hour<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Delilah's paint with the aid of their beast and so the beast is apart of their art, and it can call out to it's kin. They may imbue their painting with their predatory aura, designated as Monstrous, Seductive or Competitive when created. Any vampire viewing the painting must make an appropriate Resistance trait+Blood potency - successes roll or be affected with the Bestial, Wanton or Competitive conditions as designated by the painting's aura. The aura remains potent for 1 week per dot of blood potency.<br /> <br /> Inspiring Vision<br /> Requirements: majesty 2<br /> Roll: Intelligence+Crafts+Blood Potency taking 1 hour<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> The paintings of a delilah speak of their majesty and grace in every paint stroke and that is clear to all who behold their art. A vampire may infuse their painting with their majesty. Anyone seeing it must make a resolve+blood potency - successes roll or suffer the charmed condition relating to the artist. The painting's aura remains potent for 1 week per dot of blood potency<br /> <br /> Art Imitates life<br /> Roll: Intelligence+Crafts+Blood Potency taking 1 hour<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> The paintings of the Delilah are born of the beast and contain it's vampiric hunger. A vampire may infuse their painting with their hunger. Anyone viewing the painting must make a resolve+Blood potency roll -successes or lose 1 willpower. Once it has absorbed an amount of willpower equal to the users blood potency they artist may touch the painting, drawing out the willpower and giving themselves the inspired condition on one skill roll designated and depicted in the painting's creation. The user may be inspired by only one painting at a time. The painting maintains potency for 1 week per dot of blood potency and loses all gathered will if it expires.<br /> <br /> Cursed Portrait<br /> Requires: Auspex 2<br /> Roll: Intelligence+Crafts+Blood Potency - Resolve+Blood Potency taking 1 hour<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae per 2 successes (minimum 1 vitae)<br /> You may paint a portrait of a victim you have previously analysed with Uncanny Perception, representing a likeness of both their body and spirit. The artist then whispers to depiction of their target who can then be afflicted with a number of effects equal to successes, the portrait changing to depict the resulting effect. Once all the curses have been exhausted the painting smudges into an unrecognizable mess.<br /> -Cause a vampire to wretch and vomit blood, losing 1 point of vitae<br /> -Whisper a mad and terrible secret to the victim causing them to gain the spooked condition<br /> -Hex the victim causing 1 lethal damage<br /> -Lash out with your beast against the victim, resolving the conflict normally<br /> <br /> Painting's Eyes<br /> Requires: Auspex 4<br /> Roll: Intelligence+Crafts+Blood Potency - Resolve+Blood Potency taking 1 hour<br /> Cost: 2 Vitae<br /> You may paint a portrait of a victim you have previously analysed with Uncanny Perception, representing a likeness of both their body and spirit. The artist may then stare at the target within the portrait, going into a trance, allowing them to see and hear the target as though they were in the presence of the target, Auspex may reveal the supernatural observer provoking a clash of wills. Once the artist ends the trance ends the portrait smudges into an unrecognizable mess.<br /> <br /> Portrait of the soul<br /> Requires: Auspex 5, Blood Potency 4, Cursed Portrait<br /> Roll: Intelligence+Crafts+Blood Potency taking 1 hour<br /> Cost: 5 Vitae<br /> You may create a painting that can trap a target within the paint upon it's canvas. The Artist paints an indistinct figure and then designates a target either a specific person or type of creature (Prince Adrian, ghouls, humans) and if that target locks eyes with the figure in the frame they must make a Composure+Resolve+Supernatural Tolerance roll - successes. Failure traps the target within the painting until the painting is destroyed, as the target takes the place of the indistinct figure. Interestingly while strix (and any ephemeral entities) cannot be designated as targets, if a target is possessed the entity makes the roll and is trapped in the target's place, a fact the Delilah progenitor has not disclosed at this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 05-07-2017, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:46:46-07:00","id":1089186,"title":"","content":"I noticed that the last effect of Cursed Portrait and Truth in Art are somewhat similar. Why not move all the effects to Truth in Art?<br /> Make it a power that lets you activate it for all people who see the painting or just a specific target.<br /> <br /> Also, on Cursed Portrait, sucesses number of effects seems too powerfull if you can choose the same effect twice or more times. Is that an option? Cause I'm pretty sure you can almost kill anyone with 3~4 effects of Hex damage. My take on it would be changing the effects to happen at intervals of 1 hour.<br /> <br /> Something like that:<br /> Cursed Portrait<br /> Requires: Auspex 2<br /> Roll: Intelligence+Crafts+Blood Potency - Resolve+Blood Potency taking 1 hour<br /> <b>Cost: 1 Vitae per 2 sucesses (minimum of 1 Vitae)</b><br /> You may paint a portrait of a victim you have previously analysed with Uncanny Perception, representing a likeness of both their body and spirit. The artist then whispers to depiction of their target who will be afflicted with an effect for a number of hours equal to successes, the portrait changing to depict the resulting effect every hour.<br /> Once the time has passed the painting smudges into an unrecognizable mess. The Delilah can set less hours than the number of sucess acquired for less expenditure of Vitae.<br /> Effects:<br /> - Cause a vampire to wretch and vomit blood, losing 1 point of vitae per hour.<br /> - Whisper a mad and terrible secret to the victim causing them to gain the spooked condition per the duration of the painting. They cannot resolve the condition while the power is on effect, but gain Beats normally.<br /> - Hex the victim causing 1 lethal damage per hour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:56:11-07:00","id":1089192,"title":"","content":"hmm I agree that the damage is too high (I based it on the cursed effigy merit in hurt locker) and the effects are separated as they are able to affect targets differently, I liked the idea of a painting being able to provoke reactions from a vampire's beast the same way art can provoke emotions in people and I like cursed portrait causing damage as it allows one to cause harm from an unknown source and the fear that could create. The per hour idea is interesting but really abusable as a powerful vampire could keep 